      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the main motivation for this CL is performance (parallelizing Starlark rule execution), would it make sense to prioritize getting the core Starlark functionality working end-to-end first and defer this optimization until later? Keeping resolution synchronous for now avoids adding concurrency complexity (`STATE_RESOLVING`, thread-safety hazards, and potential regressions on non-Starlark builds) while the feature is still being built out.\n\nIf the builtin target evaluation part (`rust_target(session)` / `is_builtin()`) is needed now for follow-up CLs (e.g. https://gn-review.googlesource.com/c/gn/+/29260), splitting that out separately could keep things simpler.",
      "revId": "aaa268f75c3fcac4bcd7e3cd26959576948adc4c",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
