      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Review from Jetski] Checking `has_starlark_session()` inside the worker lambda (line 585) means that even for regular non-Starlark GN builds, every `Target` now transitions to `STATE_RESOLVING` and has to round-trip through the worker pool and a main-thread `PostTask` before `CompleteItemResolution()` unblocks dependents. Previously, dependents were unblocked synchronously on the main thread while only `RunChecksAfterResolution` ran in the background.\n\nFor deep dependency graphs (e.g. Chromium), adding a main \u003c-\u003e worker round-trip per dependency level could regress non-Starlark `gn gen` latency. Could we check `has_starlark_session()` here (or at the start of `ScheduleBackgroundTargetResolution`) and keep the synchronous `CompleteItemResolution` fast path when Starlark is disabled?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "aaa268f75c3fcac4bcd7e3cd26959576948adc4c",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
