      "message": "[Review from Jetski] Now that `execute_rule_impl` (which calls `self.evaluated.set(...)`) runs concurrently across worker threads while `\u0026\u0027static Target` is shared via `unsafe impl Sync for Target`, using non-thread-safe `std::cell::OnceCell` is fragile — any read path that reaches a `Target` without a strict happens-before edge (e.g. via `Session::targets` or validation/gen_deps edges) would be a data race / UB.\n\nCould we switch this to `std::sync::OnceLock`? Reads via `get()` are just an acquire load, so the overhead is negligible while making `Target::evaluated` genuinely thread-safe.",
